  "security_implications": "The secret_key register is zeroized on asynchronous reset and directly loaded from secret_key_d every cycle. If secret_key_d is ever uncontrolled, stale, or attacker-influenced around reset release, a hostile key can be loaded and used for subsequent HMAC operations. The lack of a write-enable or key-loading handshake creates a continuous update path that must be safeguarded upstream. This chunk touches secret/key storage and reset zeroization, with direct propagation to cryptographic output if security precondition fails.",
